# Citation metadata for the WUDAPT-FUSE software repository.
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "WUDAPT-FUSE: A workstation-runnable framework for testing whether building morphology, topology, or geographic position governs within-class urban heat exposure inequality at the 100-m scale"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (this CITATION.cff) and the accompanying paper (preferred-citation below)."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yanhuo
    family-names: Luo
    email: s2134612@siswa.um.edu.my
    affiliation: "Institute for Advanced Studies, University of Malaya, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO: replace with real ORCID
repository-code: "https://github.com/s2134612-hub/WUDAPT-FUSE"
url: "https://github.com/s2134612-hub/WUDAPT-FUSE"
abstract: "WUDAPT-FUSE is a workstation-runnable analytical framework that fuses ERA5-HEAT, the Demuzere global Local Climate Zone map, WorldPop 2020 gridded population, and OpenStreetMap building footprints into a single 100-m grid, synthesises hourly UTCI fields by deviation injection, and tests four competing hypotheses (morphology, topology, hybrid form-plus-topology, geographic position) for within-class urban heat inequality using the population-weighted Pyatt–Yitzhaki Gini decomposition. Applied to three Greater Bay Area cities (Shenzhen, Guangzhou, Dongguan) across four seasons of 2020, the framework runs end-to-end in under 5 minutes on a single GPU workstation."
keywords:
  - urban heat inequality
  - Local Climate Zone
  - Universal Thermal Climate Index
  - Gini decomposition
  - Greater Bay Area
  - geographic position
  - sea breeze
  - topological data analysis
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
